<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ki Hajar Dewantara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1889–1959</span> · Also known as Soewardi Soerjaningrat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ki Hajar Dewantara, born Raden Mas Soewardi Soerjaningrat into the Pakualaman princely family of Yogyakarta, was an Indonesian nationalist and educator. Exiled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> for his writings, he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taman-siswa">Taman Siswa</a> school movement in 1922 and became independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>'s first minister of education. His birthday, 2 May, is National Education Day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ki-hajar-dewantara.jpg" alt="Ki Hajar Dewantara" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Djawa Sjinboen Sja · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ki_Hadjar_Dewantara,_Djawa_Baroe_(1943),_p5.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
